# What never enters the build context. The image only needs distro/zsh/ and
# distro/build/first_boot.sh (see the COPY lines in the Dockerfile);
# everything else is either noise sent to the Docker daemon or user
# configuration that must not be baked into /etc/skel.
#
# This file sits BESIDE the Dockerfile under the name Dockerfile.dockerignore
# - the only name a builder reads next to a `-f` Dockerfile (BuildKit) - but
# its patterns are written against the CONTEXT ROOT, the repository: they
# match ./scripts, ./distro/packs and so on, never this folder.
#
# distro/packs/ is in this list because the image no longer carries any of it:
# a pack arrives on the instance, from Windows. No COPY line reads that
# folder, so sending it would be so much noise on every build.
.git
.gitattributes
.gitignore
.github
.claude
assets
docs
src/distro/packs
LICENSE
README.md
src/windows
wsl.ps1

# Build artifacts
*.tar
*.vhdx

# A local .env.global is one machine's configuration. COPY distro/zsh would
# bake it into /etc/skel, so every distro, for every user, would inherit it.
# `**/` earns its place: a pattern without a slash only matches at the root of
# the context, while the file this protects - distro/zsh/gmake/.env.global -
# sits in a subdirectory. The two *.sample files are the committed contracts
# and they stay: `**/.env*` would have taken them along.
**/.env
**/.env.global
